    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "15824e2c_a6ed4153",
        "filename": "health/2.0/vts/functional/VtsHalHealthV2_0TargetTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 412,
      "author": {
        "id": 1319951
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-30T23:20:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "no, not really. BatteryState \u003d UNKNOWN doesn\u0027t automatically means that the battery is not there. The device will report \"UNKNOWN\" right after boot for example and might do so for some time until initialization is complete (i.e. loading battery model after POR takes some time).\n\nDuring this time current average (or instantaneous) might be available and could be used along with other measurements to determine if it\u0027s time to shutdown when/if CAPACITY_LEVEL is not implemented.",
      "parentUuid": "f07c1c23_9b3fc94c",
      "revId": "98a3e115fadb627b2a4e65883d1a50df480baad9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5be8e301_56e6cae3",
        "filename": "health/2.0/vts/functional/VtsHalHealthV2_0TargetTest.cpp",
